 in Los Angeles, California.\r\n\r\nPaula Abdul began her career in Los Angeles as a choreographer for music videos. Inevitably, she moved on to making music videos of her own. She was an MTV fixture in the 80's, but has maintained a much lower musical profile since. Occasional forays into acting for television have been attempted, with her role as a judge on the TV show \"American Idol\" being her latest claim to fame.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:67260","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":[{"active":true,"id":3011307,"name":"The Cheer Girls"}],"members":null,"namevariations":["Abdul","P. Abdul","P.Abdul","Paul Abdual","Paul Abdul","Paul J. Abdul","Paula Apdul","Paula J. Abdul","Paule Abdul","Poula Abdul","Пола Абдул","พอลล่า อับดุล","ポーラ・アブドゥル","ポーラ・アブドル","宝拉.阿芭杜","寶拉阿巴杜","폴라 압둘"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/67260-Paula-Abdul","type":"artist","urls":["http://paulaabdul.com","http://www.facebook.com/PaulaAbdul","http://www.instagram.com/paulaabdul","http://twitter.com/paulaabdul","http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paula_Abdul","http://youtube.com/user/PaulaAbdulVEVO"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/8121893/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"8121893","image":"https://i.discogs.com/6pQOVxH7V_2zVy7PmVSK5lj4xbMeScuGyLh5Xj0Ah0A/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:504/w:504/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTgxMjE4/OTMtMTY1Mjg3NTg0/My05MTU0LmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/M6vekV7479q7dVpeM1e6PPJAvvmUNYqIzpV7TFsOAW0/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTgxMjE4/OTMtMTY1Mjg3NTg0/My05MTU0LmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"Duo since 2020, hailing from Frankfurt & Leipzig, now based in Frankfurt am Main, Germany.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:8121893","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":17937933,"name":"Carsten Fluck"},{"active":true,"id":17961771,"name":"Lucas Lejeune (2)"}],"namevariations":["not.even.noticed"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/8121893-Not-Even-Noticed","type":"artist","urls":["https://soundcloud.com/not-even-noticed","https://notevennoticed.bandcamp.com/","https://www.instagram.com/not.even.noticed/"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/99356/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"99356","image":"https://i.discogs.com/NTigzAFsXtD4oB5RpwCVphddBuff9e6z-uscRmDPUFI/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTk5MzU2/LTE3ODQ1MTQ5NTQt/ODk4Ni5qcGVn.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/hzPoYcWmkP7fMRxnwfy297H_3tVffgekc1LB0vLBNOQ/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTk5MzU2/LTE3ODQ1MTQ5NTQt/ODk4Ni5qcGVn.jpeg","profile":"Russian pop girl duo formed in 2000. \r\n\r\nThe name Тату, (the Russian transliteration of \"tattoo\") originated from their decision to refuse to sign any autographs except in the form of a tattoo. A later theory claims the origin is the contraction of the Russian sentence \"Та любит ту\" (This [girl] loves that [girl]). Afterwards, the producers added the dots between the letters prior to the release of the international edition of their first album because there already existed an Australian band with the same name.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:99356","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":798749,"name":"Лена Катина"},{"active":true,"id":1864677,"name":"Юля Волкова"}],"namevariations":["T A T U","T a t u","T.A.T.U","T.A.T.U.","T.A.T.U..","T.A.Tu","T.a.T.U","T.a.T.u","TATU","Tatu","Taty","t. A. T. u.","t.A.T.U","t.A.T.u","t.A.Tu.","t.a.t.u","tA Tu","tATu","tatu","Гр. \"Тату\"","ТА ТУ","ТАТУ","ТаТу","Тату","†.a.†.u.","ｔ．Ａ．Ｔ．ｕ．"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/99356-tATu","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.facebook.com/tatuofficial","https://twitter.com/tatuofficial","http://www.youtube.com/tatu","http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/T.A.T.u.","http://vk.com/tatu","http://promodj.com/tatu","https://web.archive.org/web/20050211091903/http://www.tatu.ru/"]}},"/api/discogs/label/139430/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"139430","image":"https://i.discogs.com/xPZlWWnibA_eU4MWuNWqZnVCbY04mFzDRYlvvHs04nk/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:283/w:291/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTEzOTQz/MC0xNjA3NTcyMDMw/LTk5OTkuanBlZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/xMfH7J2vlZiMgitPmvJPcEeijgA-paNgbRpKV4uJ8qM/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTEzOTQz/MC0xNjA3NTcyMDMw/LTk5OTkuanBlZw.jpeg","profile":"French label sometimes credited just as \"L'inlassable\".","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:139430","relations":{"parentLabel":null,"sublabels":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/label/139430-Linlassable-Disque","type":"label","urls":["https://www.chezjean.fr/fr/label","http://www.linlassable.com/","https://www.facebook.com/linlassable/?ref=page_internal"]}},"/api/discogs/label/1946019/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"1946019","image":"https://i.discogs.com/w12gypuxj18MBC-9jaW_higjT_ruilgYVKgxkSqXBwg/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:464/w:494/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTE5NDYw/MTktMTYwNzIxMjYz/Ni0yODY2LnBuZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/Gb8fUquviUgiq6EjFHU1R1XTq-fIlzhEUEmdniY9Ky4/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTE5NDYw/MTktMTYwNzIxMjYz/Ni0yODY2LnBuZw.jpeg","profile":"Electronic music label based in Berlin, Germany.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:1946019","relations":{"parentLabel":null,"sublabels":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/label/1946019-Delicate-Records-2","type":"label","urls":["https://www.facebook.com/delicaterecords/","https://itsdelicaterecords.bandcamp.com/"]}},"/api/discogs/label/2927/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"2927","image":"https://i.discogs.com/IJ008OhRH62IWKaG9wbS3WPM4383DhcKS3PPRV1vZK4/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:525/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTI5Mjct/MTYzOTYzMTU3MS01/NDEzLmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/_ReypQ1rjZG0yzSUpa6OAbv3Bvld9utsa14H8BgIKDU/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTI5Mjct/MTYzOTYzMTU3MS01/NDEzLmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"Southern US based label founded by production duo [url=https://www.discogs.com/artist/51281-LA-Reid]Antonio \"L.A.\" Reid[/url] and Kenneth \"[a=Babyface]\" Edmonds. \r\nAn imprint of [l=Arista Records], LaFace scored hits throughout the 90s with a diverse stable of artists including [a=Usher], [a=Toni Braxton], [a36988], [a=OutKast], [a=Donell Jones] and [a=TLC].\r\n\r\nBy the end of the decade, Babyface was less involved with the label while still pursuing his own musical career. Antonio \"L.A.\" Reid took over from [l=Arista] co-founder and president [a=Clive Davis] as the succeeding head of the label in 2000, and most of the LaFace artists (including the recently signed rapper [a=T.I.]) went with him (though some went to Davis' newly launched [l=J Records]). This seemingly marked the end of LaFace, but in 2004, following the merger of its parent company [l=Sony BMG], the label was revitalized as one quarter of the newly rearranged [b][l=Zomba Label Group][/b] alongside [l=So So Def], [l84472] and [l=Jive]. Under the LaFace reboot, Usher, Donell Jones and P!NK rejoined while the label had recently signed [a=Ciara].\r\n\r\nLaFace Records' most prominent release to date was the 1994 TLC album, [i]CrazySexyCool[/i], which was the highest selling album by any all-female group with over 12 million copies sold in the United States alone.\r\n\r\nOn September 26, 2011, the [l=RCA Music Group] was disbanded by [l=Sony], and on October 7, LaFace, alongside its parent, [a=Arista], and sister labels, [l=Jive] and [l=J Records], were all absorbed into [l=RCA Records], bringing all of its artists to the RCA family.\r\n\r\nLabel code - LC07925 Jive\r\nLabel code - LC13517 LaFace\r\n\r\nFor unofficial and counterfeit releases please use [l=LaFace Records (2)].","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:2927","relations":{"parentLabel":{"id":29073,"name":"Sony Music Entertainment"},"sublabels":[{"id":19935,"name":"LaFace"},{"id":42663,"name":"Tony Mercedes Records"}]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/label/2927-LaFace-Records","type":"label","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LaFace_Records"]}},"/api/discogs/label/297/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"297","image":"https://i.discogs.com/bmMAyLVCv1lKBWekYUAGdQiY-pD2AYLnFf_ORta5WCU/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:598/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTI5Ny0x/NDg0NDA4ODE3LTIw/MzcuanBlZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/MaUq0AdsBdKbXzT6_QFv5h_k9QXzDh9nq5KwFxZG-uE/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTI5Ny0x/NDg0NDA4ODE3LTIw/MzcuanBlZw.jpeg","profile":"Dance music-focused imprint founded as Full Frequency Range Recordings in 1986 under the umbrella of [l=London Records] with [a=Pete Tong] as A&R and [a=Phil Howells] as assistant. Early releases included Lil Louis' French Kiss, D Mob's We Call It Acieed and Salt-N-Pepa's Push It. Albums from Orbital, Goldie and All Saints followed in the 1990s. [a=Nick Raphael (2)] started at the label as product manager and later became label manager. \r\n\r\nIn 1979 when Polygram Records purchased the ailing Decca Record company, London was just another document trademark gathering dust. Upon its revival and rebirth three years later it took up where it had left off, licensing young black American acts (New Edition, Rockers Revenge) and founding its own roster beginning with Blancmange and Bananarama. At the time what differentiated London from other \"Major\" record companies was its incredibly high proportion of chart entries and the esteem in which it held the then scorned \"dance music\". With the development of the London roster and the addition of rock acts such as the Hothouse Flowers and Then Jericho there was a danger that the dance focus of the early London would be lost, and a decision has been taken to separate the company into two labels, FFRR and London.\r\n\r\nThe original FFRR was a trademark of Decca. It was launched in 1947 to mark the advent of a new era in high fidelity sound, and it was later incorporated into the London logo. The new (1987–present) FFRR is an independent dance label under the guidance of Head of A&R Pete Tong, responsible for continuing the great tradition of dance music at London Records.\r\n\r\nAlthough the company name FFRR Records Ltd. first appeared on releases in 1986, the standard London logos were used until 1987. Such releases, even if they have an old-style \"ffrr\" badge embedded in the London logos, should only be filed under [l=London Records]. A new logo for the dance imprint first appeared on releases in 1987. It incorporated elements of the classic \"ffrr\" high-fidelity marks that had been part of the [l=Decca] and London branding since the 1940s, yet it is a unique logo, with a key difference being that it normally appears by itself and contains the words [i]Full Frequency Range Recordings[/i] (not [i]Recording[/i], and not [i]American Recordings[/i] or [i]British Recordings[/i]). The [b]ffrr[/b] high-fidelity mark (normally paired with a London or Decca logo) is not catalogued in the database as a distinct label or series; for releases with that branding, please only enter the label as [l=London Records] or [l=Decca] as appropriate, and mention ffrr in the release notes.\r\n\r\nFrom 1990 on, the imprint was affiliated with both FFRR Records Ltd and former immediate parent [l26831].\r\nPete Tong relaunched the label in 2011 and it now sits as a sub label of [l=Parlophone] within the wider [l=Warner Music Group].\r\n\r\nLabel head from October 2019 to April 2024: [a=Andy Daniell], with [a=Evie Grain] (ex-BMG) as marketing lead from 2021.\r\nThe label was rebranded in February 2021 with an updated logo by [a=Trevor Jackson].\r\n\r\n[b]DJ[/b] on the catalog numbers generally denotes a prom